{"id":"staff-federal-gifts","title":"Federal campaign gifts from the staff of City payees","tier":"CLEARED","question":"Do people who work for organisations the City pays give to federal campaigns in ways that look organised by the employer?","finding":"Little to see. Staff of 125 private organisations paid $1 million or more by the City gave $4.0 million to federal committees between 2017 and 2026, and $1.3 million of that (32%) was payroll giving to the employer's own political committee. Only 3 same-day groups of three or more people from one employer went to a single candidate. Their staff gave $8,460 of the $523,915 that San Francisco residents gave Supervisor Connie Chan's 2026 campaign for Congress, and $28,725 of the $2,213,556 given to State Senator Scott Wiener's.","how":"Read 1,826,165 itemised gifts by San Francisco residents in the Federal Election Commission's files for the 2018 to 2026 cycles, leaving out memo entries and the duplicate copy filed by conduits. The employer written on each gift was matched, after tidying the name, to private payees the City paid $1 million or more in fiscal years 2019 to 2026 (public bodies and universities left out). A same-day group is three or more people from one employer giving $500 or more each, $3,000 or more together, to one candidate's committee on one date. The employer's own committee is a political committee whose name starts with the employer's name. A senior officer is named only when the organisation is a City-funded nonprofit and the federal record shows $5,000 or more in one two-year cycle.","limits":"The City’s contractor rules do not govern federal gifts. The employer is whatever the donor wrote, so this is a name match: staff who wrote a different name are missed and unrelated firms with the same name can be caught. Only gifts large enough to be itemised appear. People who work together often give together after a fundraiser; a same-day group is a reason to ask whether anyone was reimbursed, nothing more. The 2026 file was dated 8 November 2026 and is incomplete.","columns":[{"k":"org","t":"Employer as written on the gift","type":"org"},{"k":"cityPaid","t":"City paid, FY2019-26","type":"usd"},{"k":"gifts","t":"Federal gifts by staff, 2017-26","type":"usd"},{"k":"donors","t":"Donors","type":"int"},{"k":"viaOwnPac","t":"Of which to the employer's own committee","type":"usd"},{"k":"topRecipient","t":"Largest recipient","type":"text"},{"k":"sameDay","t":"Largest same-day group to a candidate","type":"text"},{"k":"localSeat","t":"To the Chan or Wiener 2026 campaigns","type":"usd"},{"k":"officers","t":"Senior officers giving $5,000 or more in a cycle","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"cityPaid":366301300,"gifts":820541,"donors":425,"viaOwnPac":742502,"topRecipient":"PG&E Corporation Employees Energypac ($742,502)","sameDay":"3 people, $7,000, 2017-04-27, to Stabenow for US Senate","localSeat":1000,"officers":"","org":"Pacific Gas & Electric Co"},{"cityPaid":237686937,"gifts":307064,"donors":536,"viaOwnPac":295661,"topRecipient":"Wells Fargo and Company Employee Pac (aka Wells Fargo Employee Pac) ($183,045)","sameDay":"","localSeat":1750,"officers":"","org":"Wells Fargo Bank N A"},{"cityPaid":1375576,"gifts":287008,"donors":232,"viaOwnPac":0,"topRecipient":"Fight for the People Pac ($40,899)","sameDay":"","localSeat":4850,"officers":"","org":"Kaiser Permanente"},{"cityPaid":3163794,"gifts":247515,"donors":10,"viaOwnPac":0,"topRecipient":"Ab Pac ($225,000)","sameDay":"","localSeat":null,"officers":"","org":"San Francisco Museum of Modern Art","orgKey":"SAN FRANCISCO MUSEUM MODERN ART"},{"cityPaid":26431945,"gifts":208310,"donors":62,"viaOwnPac":193075,"topRecipient":"Deloitte Political Action Committee ($193,075)","sameDay":"","localSeat":null,"officers":"","org":"Deloitte Consulting LLP"},{"cityPaid":5422900,"gifts":193896,"donors":60,"viaOwnPac":0,"topRecipient":"Harris Victory Fund ($23,448)","sameDay":"3 people, $4,200, 2017-11-27, to Ralph Baxter for Congress","localSeat"